  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Consider the following operations on a triple of integers. In one operation, you should:\n\n\nChoose an integer ddd and an arithmetic operation ― either addition or multiplication.\nChoose a subset of elements of the triple.\nApply the arithmetic operation to each of the chosen elements, i.e. either add ddd to each of them or multiply each of them by ddd.\nFor example, if we have a triple (3,5,7)(3, 5, 7)(3,5,7), we may choose to add 333 to the first and third element, and we get (6,5,10)(6, 5, 10)(6,5,10) using one operation.\n\nYou are given an initial triple (p,q,r)(p, q, r)(p,q,r) and a target triple (a,b,c)(a, b, c)(a,b,c). Find the minimum number of operations needed to transform (p,q,r)(p, q, r)(p,q,r) into (a,b,c)(a, b, c)(a,b,c).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1,0001 \\le T \\le 1,0001≤T≤1,000",
      "∣p∣,∣q∣,∣r∣,∣a∣,∣b∣,∣c∣≤109|p|, |q|, |r|, |a|, |b|, |c| \\le 10^9∣p∣,∣q∣,∣r∣,∣a∣,∣b∣,∣c∣≤109",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (10 points):** ∣p∣,∣q∣,∣r∣,∣a∣,∣b∣,∣c∣≤10|p|, |q|, |r|, |a|, |b|, |c| \\le 10∣p∣,∣q∣,∣r∣,∣a∣,∣b∣,∣c∣≤10"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains three space-separated integers ppp, qqq and rrr.\nThe second line contains three space-separated integers aaa, bbb and ccc.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, print a single line containing one integer ― the minimum required number of operations.",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n3 5 7\n6 5 10\n8 6 3\n9 7 8",
        "output": "1\n2",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nExample case 1: We add 333 to the first and third element of (3,5,7)(3, 5, 7)(3,5,7) to form (6,5,10)(6, 5, 10)(6,5,10).\nExample case 2: We can add 111 to each element to form (9,7,4)(9, 7, 4)(9,7,4) and then multiply the third element by 222."
      }
    ]
